  "content": "Slight drop in gold price\nOnlinekhabar\nFriday, October 10, 2025\n0\nComments\nPhoto: Unsplash/\nsuradeach saetang\nKathmandu, October 10\nThe price of gold has slightly fallen in the domestic bullion market today. The price of the yellow metal has dropped by Rs 4,200 per tola (11.66 grammes) today as compared to the price on Thursday.\nThe Federation of Nepal Gold and Silver Dealers’ Association stated that gold which was traded at Rs 239,200 per tola on Thursday is being traded at Rs 235,000 today.\nHowever, the price of silver has increased today. Silver was traded at Rs 3,025 per tola on Thursday. It is being traded at Rs 3,085 today, the Federation stated.\nThe price of gold is 3,058 USD in the international market today, according to the international media.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nBP Highway\nFlowers\nnational women team\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\n4 days ago\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n4 days ago\nGold price reaches record high\n3 weeks ago\nGold price hikes by Rs 1,100 per tola\n3 weeks ago\nGold prices hit new record, rise by Rs 1,600 per tola\n1 month ago\nGold price hits record high at Rs 205,900 per tola\n1 month ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n14 hours ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n14 hours ago\nFestival\nFlowers ready for Tihar Festival (Photos)\n14 hours ago\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n2 days ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n2 days ago",
